$(
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
  The matrix algebra
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=

  The main result of this subsection are the theorems showing that
  ` ( N Mat R ) ` is a ring (see ~ matring ) and an associative algebra (see
  ~ matassa ).  Additionally, theorems for the identity matrix and transposed
  matrices are provided.

$)

