$(
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
  The matrix adjugate/adjunct
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
$)

  $c maAdju $.
  $c minMatR1 $.

  $( Syntax for the matrix adjugate/adjunct function. $)
  cmadu $a class maAdju $.

  $( Syntax for the minor matrices of a square matrix. $)
  cminmar1 $a class minMatR1 $.

  ${
    $d n r m i j k l $.
    $( Define the adjugate or adjunct (matrix of cofactors) of a square matrix.
       This definition gives the standard cofactors, however the internal
       minors are not the standard minors, see definition in [Lang] p. 518.
       (Contributed by Stefan O'Rear, 7-Sep-2015.)  (Revised by SO,
       10-Jul-2018.) $)
    df-madu $a |- maAdju = ( n e. _V , r e. _V |->
        ( m e. ( Base ` ( n Mat r ) ) |-> ( i e. n , j e. n |->
          ( ( n maDet r ) ` ( k e. n , l e. n |-> if ( k = j , if ( l = i ,
            ( 1r ` r ) , ( 0g ` r ) ) , ( k m l ) ) ) ) ) ) ) $.
  $}

  ${
    $d n r m i j k l $.
    $( Define the matrices whose determinants are the minors of a square
       matrix.  In contrast to the standard definition of minors, a row is
       replaced by 0's and one 1 instead of deleting the column and row (e.g.,
       definition in [Lang] p. 515).  By this, the determinant of such a matrix
       is equal to the minor determined in the standard way (as determinant of
       a submatrix, see ~ df-subma - note that the matrix is transposed
       compared with the submatrix defined in ~ df-subma , but this does not
       matter because the determinants are the same, see ~ mdettpos ).  Such
       matrices are used in the definition of an adjunct of a square matrix,
       see ~ df-madu .  (Contributed by AV, 27-Dec-2018.) $)
    df-minmar1 $a |- minMatR1 = ( n e. _V , r e. _V |->
       ( m e. ( Base ` ( n Mat r ) ) |-> ( k e. n , l e. n |->
         ( i e. n , j e. n |-> if ( i = k ,
                if ( j = l , ( 1r ` r ) , ( 0g ` r ) ) , ( i m j ) ) ) ) ) ) $.
  $}

