$(
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
  Ring isomorphism between polynomial matrices and polynomials over matrices
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
<HTML>
The main result of this section is Theorem ~ pmmpric , which shows that the
ring of polynomial matrices and the ring of polynomials having matrices as
coefficients (called "polynomials over matrices" in the following) are
isomorphic:<br>
` ( Poly1 `` ( N Mat R ) ) ~= ( N Mat ( Poly1 `` R ) ) `
<br><br>

Or in a more common notation:<br>
` ( N Mat ( Poly1 `` R ) ) ` corresponds to
M(n, R[[t]), the ring of n x n polynomial matrices over the ring R.<br>
` ( Poly1 `` ( N Mat R ) ) ` corresponds to M(n, R)[[t], the
polynomial ring over the ring of n x n matrices with entries in ring R.
<br><br>
` T = ( m e. B |-> ( Q gsum ( k e. NN0
|-> ( ( m decompPMat k ) .* ( k .^ X ) ) ) ) ) `
<br><br>
with ` B = ( Base `` ( N Mat ( Poly1 `` R ) ) ) ` and ` ( m decompPMat k )
= ( i e. N , j e. N |-> ( ( coe1 ` ( i m j ) ) ` k ) ) ) ` is an isomorphism
between these rings:<br>
<br>
` T : B -1-1-onto-> L ` with ` L = ( Base `` ( Poly1
`` ( N Mat R ) ) ) ` (see ~ pm2mpf1o and ~ pm2mprngiso ), and<br>
<br>
` I = ( p e. L |-> ( i e. N , j e. N |-> ( P gsum ( k e. NN0
|-> ( ( i ( ( coe1 ` p ) ` k ) j ) .x. ( k E Y ) ) ) ) ) ) `
<br><br>
is the corresponding inverse function:<br>
<br>
` ( T `` ( I `` O ) ) = O ) ` (see ~ mp2pm2mp ).
<br><br>

In this section, the following conventions are mostly used:
<ul>
<li>` R ` is a (unital) ring (see ~ df-ring )</li>
<li>` P = ( Poly1 `` R ) ` is the polynomial algebra over (the ring) ` R ` (see
      ~ df-ply1 )
  <ul>
  <li>` K = ( Base `` P ) ` is its base set (see ~ df-base )</li>
  <li>` Y = ( var1 `` R ) ` is its variable (see ~ df-vr1 )</li>
  <li>` .x. = ( .s `` P ) ` is its scalar multiplication (see ~ df-vsca or
        ~ lmodvscl )</li>
  <li>` E = ( .g `` ( mulGrp `` P ) ) ` is its exponentiation (see ~ df-mulg )
  </li>
  </ul></li>
<li>` A = ( N Mat R ) ` is the algebra of N x N matrices over (the ring) ` R `
      (see ~ df-mat )</li>
<li>` C = ( N Mat P ) ` is the algebra of N x N matrices over (the polynomial
 ring) ` P `.
  <ul>
  <li>` B = ( Base `` C ) ` is its base set</li>
  <li>` M e. B ` is a concrete polynomial matrix</li>
  </ul></li>
<li>` Q = ( Poly1 `` A ) ` is the polynomial algebra over (the matrix ring)
      ` A `.
  <ul>
  <li>` L = ( Base `` Q ) ` is its base set</li>
  <li>` O e. L ` is a concrete polynomial with matrix coefficients</li>
  <li>` X = ( var1 `` A ) ` is its variable</li>
  <li>` .* = ( .s `` Q ) ` is its scalar multiplication</li>
  <li>` .^ = ( .g `` ( mulGrp `` Q ) ) ` is its exponentiation</li></ul></li>
</ul></HTML>
$)

  $c pMatToMatPoly $.

  $( Extend class notation with the transformation of a polynomial matrix into
     a polynomial over matrices. $)
